# Fun Core Custom-Development Commercial License

**English** (this file) · [简体中文](LICENSE.custom.zh.md)

## Special Notice

The Fun language core (including but not limited to `fun.exe`, `fun.dll`, and their complete source code) may be freely used, modified, and studied. However, if you:

- Make **substantial modifications** to the Fun core and redistribute the modified version **closed-source** as part of your own commercial product; or
- Build a **derivative work** based on the Fun core (such as a customized interpreter or a dedicated runtime) and sell it under a commercial license; or
- Embed a **customized version** of the Fun core into your hardware device, SaaS service, or commercial software and distribute it closed-source;

then you must purchase a **Custom-Development Commercial License**.

### Free usage scenarios (no license required)

The following cases do not require purchasing a commercial license:

- You modify the Fun core, but publish the modified version publicly under an **open-source license (such as MIT, GPL)**.
- You modify the Fun core, but use it only for **internal tools, testing, or learning**, without distributing it externally.
- You directly use the official `fun.exe` / `fun.dll` (unmodified) and use or redistribute it under the MIT license.

### What the commercial license grants

After purchasing the Custom-Development Commercial License, you receive:

- **Full permission** to customize, modify, and distribute the Fun core closed-source
- **Perpetual usage rights** to your customized version (not dependent on later versions)
- Official **technical support and prioritized response**
- Optional: **merging your custom modifications back into the mainline** (subject to our evaluation)
- Not included: exclusive rights to the public release of `fun.exe` / `fun.dll` (other customers may still purchase the same license)

### Pricing and how to obtain it

The Custom-Development Commercial License is a **one-time license**, priced per project or per company. The specific price is determined by the following factors:

- The scope and depth of the modifications
- Whether kernel-core components are involved (parser, GC, FFI layer)
- Whether additional technical support or training is needed

Please contact us for a quote:

 zwd@funlang.org

---

> **In simple terms**: You may modify the Fun core freely within your company and use it as you wish. But if you want to sell the modified version as your own product to others, that is essentially "commercially distributing my core code", so please pay.
